{"topicSections":[{"title":"Data formatting","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DiscreteFormatStyle","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/ParseableFormatStyle"],"anchor":"Data-formatting"},{"title":"Data parsing","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/ParseableFormatStyle","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/ParseStrategy"],"anchor":"Data-parsing"},{"title":"Internationalization","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Locale"],"anchor":"Internationalization"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Fundamentals","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/NumbersDataAndBasicValues","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/StringsAndText","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Collections","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DatesAndTimes","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FiltersAndSorting"],"anchor":"Fundamentals"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"FoundationEssentials defines the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol to establish conventions for formatting a given type as some kind of output type, typically a "},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Similarly, the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/ParseStrategy"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol provides an API for converting a representation back to the represented type, such as converting a numeric string to an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Decimal"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"While FoundationEssentials defines the core protocols, most implementations of "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/ParseStrategy","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" exist in the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FoundationInternationalization"},{"type":"text","text":" module."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FoundationInternationalization"},{"type":"text","text":" also extends types in both "},{"code":"FoundationEssentials","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the Swift Standard Library to add formatting and parsing support.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When you import ","type":"text"},{"code":"FoundationInternationalization","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", you have two general approaches to perform formatting of supported types:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Call ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"formatted()"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"formatted(_:)"},{"text":" on an instance of the type, optionally passing in a customized ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FormatStyle"},{"text":" appropriate to the type. These methods, defined by extensions in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FoundationInternationalization"},{"text":", are useful for performing one-off formatting with default styles or slightly-customized styles. For example, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var string123 = Double(1.23).formatted()"},{"text":" creates the string ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1.23"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"format(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" on an instance of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FormatStyle"},{"type":"text","text":", passing in the type you want to format. This method, defined by the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FormatStyle"},{"type":"text","text":" itself, makes sense when you customize a style and want to format many instances with it. For example, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var string456 = FloatingPointFormatStyle<Double>().format(4.56)"},{"type":"text","text":" creates the string "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"4.56"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The arrangement is similar with parsing:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(strategy:)"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"init(_:format:lenient:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to create instance of a type from its formatted representation. For example, to create a "},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" from the string "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1.23"},{"type":"text","text":", you could use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var oneTwoThree = try Double(\"1.23\", format: FloatingPointFormatStyle<Double>())"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call "},{"code":"parse(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on an instance of the ","type":"text"},{"code":"ParseStrategy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to initialize an instance of the output type. For example, ","type":"text"},{"code":"var fourFiveSix = try FloatingPointFormatStyle<Double>().parseStrategy.parse(\"4.56\")","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" creates a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" equal to ","type":"text"},{"code":"4.56","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/foundationessentials\/dataformatting"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Convert numbers, dates, measurements, and other values to and from locale-aware string representations.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"title":"Data formatting","modules":[{"name":"FoundationEssentials"}],"roleHeading":"API Collection","role":"collectionGroup"},"kind":"article","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DataFormatting"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://FoundationEssentials/documentation/FoundationEssentials/ParseStrategy":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ParseStrategy"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ParseStrategy","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ParseStrategy","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that parses an input representation, such as a formatted string, into a provided data type."}],"url":"\/documentation\/foundationessentials\/parsestrategy","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/ParseStrategy"},"doc://FoundationEssentials/documentation/FoundationEssentials/NumbersDataAndBasicValues":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/NumbersDataAndBasicValues","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","url":"\/document